%META:TOPICPARENT{name="WebHome"}%
---+ Glossary

%TOC%

$ *All cells*: CGV Web display mode (=V= hotkey) that reveals every GLB cell of the enabled sub-detectors, painting cells with no XML hit using the coldest colour of their sub-detector palette. Bypasses the energy threshold and cluster filters for display.

$ *ATLAS*: A Toroidal LHC ApparatuS. One of the two general-purpose experiments at the CERN LHC.

$ *ATHENA*: ATLAS' offline software framework (Gaudi-based). Produces the JiveXML that CGV Web reads.

$ *ATLANTIS*: The Java event display. Source of the live event feed consumed by CGV Web (=atlas-live.cern.ch=).

$ *ATLAS-ID (compact)*: A 32-bit integer packing =(subDet, side, sampling, η-bin, φ-bin)= for every calorimeter cell. Decoded by CGV Web's WASM parser.

$ *Anti-k_t*: The standard ATLAS jet clustering algorithm. Jet collections like =AntiKt4EMTopoJets_xAOD= use it.

$ *Cell*: A single readout channel of a calorimeter sampling.

$ *Cinema mode*: CGV Web display state (=C= hotkey) that hides the UI and rotates the camera around the detector; with _Guided tour_ enabled, the rotation is replaced by a scripted fly-through.

$ *Cluster*: A topological grouping of adjacent cells produced by ATHENA's =CaloTopoCluster=. Drawn as dashed red outlines.

$ *Electron*: Charged-lepton candidate. Matched track is recoloured red (e&minus;) or green (e+); a sprite floats halfway along the track.

$ *Jet*: Anti-k_t reconstructed jet from a configurable collection. Drawn as a dashed orange &eta;/&phi; line.

$ *Collision HUD*: Top-left overlay that mirrors the left-panel collision footer (run, event, lumi block, timestamp, version). Auto-visible when the sidebar is unpinned or cinema mode is active.

$ *EB / LB*: Extended / Long barrel &mdash; the two tile-calorimeter cylinders.

$ *EMB / EMEC*: EM Barrel / EM End-Cap &mdash; the LAr electromagnetic calorimeters.

$ *FCAL*: Forward Calorimeter &mdash; three LAr modules at very high pseudorapidity (=η= 3.1&ndash;4.9).

$ *GeoModel*: ATLAS' unified detector-geometry description. The source-of-truth for CGV Web's =CaloGeometry.glb.gz=.

$ *Ghost*: An inactive support or cryostat volume. Rendered semi-transparent for spatial context.

$ *GLB / glTF*: Binary / JSON forms of the Khronos 3D asset format. Used for the packaged geometry.

$ *HEC*: Hadronic End-Cap calorimeter (LAr-based, 4 wheels).

$ *JiveXML*: XML event format used by ATLANTIS and CGV Web. See [[EventData]].

$ *MET*: Missing transverse energy. Drawn as a hot pink arrow in the (x, y) plane, with a =&nu;= label past the cone.

$ *Minimap*: The 2D &eta; / &phi; heatmap (top-left of the canvas, =Shift+M=). Doubles as a region picker. See [[Minimap]].

$ *Muon*: Charged-lepton candidate from the muon spectrometer. Matched =CombinedMuonTrack= is recoloured blue; a =&mu;&minus;= / =&mu;+= sprite sits at the outer end of the track.

$ *P97*: The 97th percentile of the current event's cell energies for a given sub-detector. Used as the auto ceiling of each threshold slider.

$ *Photon*: Neutral candidate drawn as a Feynman-style yellow spring landing on the first visible cell along the photon's path.

$ *Sampling*: A depth layer inside a calorimeter (=EMB1=, =EMB2=, =TileA=, etc.).

$ *Seam (&phi;)*: The minimap's vertical line that marks where the &phi; cylinder is cut. Slide it away from a cluster that straddles &plusmn;&pi; to centre the cluster in one region rectangle.

$ *Slicer*: A cylindrical-wedge carve gizmo (=Shift+S=). Hides every cell whose centre lies inside the cut volume without removing the sub-detector from the scene.

$ *Tau*: Hadronic tau candidate. Drawn as a purple dashed &eta;/&phi; line; one =&tau;= sprite per matched daughter track (three for three-prong taus).

$ *Tile*: Scintillating-tile hadronic calorimeter forming the central barrel of ATLAS.

$ *Track*: Inner-detector reconstructed trajectory. Drawn as thin yellow lines (recoloured red / green / blue / purple if matched to an electron / muon / tau).

$ *Vertex*: Primary, pile-up or secondary (b-tag) interaction point. Drawn as a small sphere at fixed pixel size on screen.

$ *View level (L1 / L2 / L3)*: Three-tier detail selector. L1 = cells + raw tracks; L2 = + clusters; L3 = + particles (default).

$ *WASM*: WebAssembly &mdash; low-level bytecode format used by the Rust ATLAS-ID parser shipped in =parser/pkg/=.

$ *WebGL2*: OpenGL ES 3.0 bindings for browsers. Required by Three.js and by CGV Web.

$ *η (eta)*: Pseudorapidity, =η = &minus;ln tan(θ/2)=.

$ *φ (phi)*: Azimuthal angle around the beam axis.

